# Plan: the wordcount command

A stint works this file top to bottom. Each iteration, a fresh agent with no
memory reads this plan and the progress log, does the first unchecked task,
checks it off, and commits. Everything it needs to act is here, including
the Working notes below.

## Done when

Every criterion under `## Done when` in `WORKSTREAM.md` holds.

## When the sources do not settle it

Do not stop, and do not decide silently. Take the smallest step that keeps
the check gate green, record it as a judgment call in the progress log, and
carry on. The sources win, even where you see a better idea. Stay inside
your task.

## Working notes

- The check gate is `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests`.

## Tasks

- [ ] Add `wordcount.py`: count the words of FILE, or of standard input when
      no FILE is given, and print the number.
      Verify: `printf 'a b\nc\n' | python3 wordcount.py` prints `3`.
- [ ] Add `tests/test_wordcount.py` covering FILE and standard input.
      Verify: the check gate passes and runs the new tests.

<!-- [ ] checkpoint -->

- [ ] Add `--lines`, and its test.
      Verify: `printf 'a b\nc\n' | python3 wordcount.py --lines` prints `2`.
- [ ] Handle a missing FILE as the head file says, with a test; add the
      `## wordcount` section to `README.md`.
      Verify: `python3 wordcount.py nope; echo $?` prints the error and `1`.

